    <!-- ===================== ABOUT ===================== -->
    <string name="about_title">ABOUT</string>
    <string name="about_body">Neurio is a local-network game streaming prototype.\n\n
        The host phone runs the real game locally, captures its screen with MediaProjection,
        encodes it with the hardware H.264 encoder and pushes the compressed stream straight to
        the client phone over Wi-Fi. The client decodes with the hardware decoder and renders it
        full screen, then sends its touch input back.\n\n
        The game is never transferred: no APK, no OBB, no data copy, no cloud server.</string>
    <string name="about_limitations_title">Honest platform limits</string>
    <string name="about_limitations">• Input: Android cannot inject touches into another app without an
        accessibility service (or root / system privileges). The app ships an accessibility injector
        that performs real gestures, plus a visualiser and a root fallback.\n
        • Audio: internal audio capture needs Android 10+ and the target game must allow playback
        capture. Games with anti-cheat / DRM usually block it — video keeps working.\n
        • Capture: MediaProjection shows a user-facing consent dialog every session; some secure
        surfaces block capture entirely.\n
        • Everything is LAN-only: there is no external server in the loop.</string>
